nnah Pingree over Republican Bobby Charles. Polling since June has consistently shown Pingree ahead by eight to fourteen points, with recent surveys averaging about eleven. Rating outlets uniformly call the race Solid or Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price a Democratic win around 95 percent. Pingree also holds a fundraising edge, raising roughly twice as much as Charles, and picked up an endorsement from Senator Angus King.\n\nCharles has kept the contest active, sparring with Pingree over spending and potential conflicts in the first televised debate and proposing to tap the state's Rainy Day Fund for heating costs. Independent Rick Bennett is on the ballot with modest resources, and his share could matter under Maine's ranked-choice system. Even so, every recent poll shows a solid Pingree lead with little sign of movement, leaving the race firmly in the Democratic column in the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9653, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9728, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 10.5}]}